        name = "out"
        type = "Uandle"
        dir = "out"
      },
    ]
    attrs = []
    ret = "Status"
  },
  {
    name = "interrupt_map"
    brief = "Writes into |out| the number interrupt_create takes for the interrupt source the platform names."
    doc = [
      "An interrupt line is named by the kernel's own number for it, which no",
      "program computes (interrupt_create). This gives the number of the line",
      "made for |source|, the platform's own number for it: the number the",
      "firmware gives a pin of the root interrupt controller, a global system",
      "interrupt (GSI) on a platform that follows ACPI. It is not a legacy",
      "device's ISA IRQ number: which pin such a device is on is for whoever",
      "reads the firmware's tables to say (the ACPI route service,",
      "ours.acpi.Route), and the kernel is given the pin. It is for that one",
      "component, and so needs the root of the interrupt lines: |resource|",
      "must be the root of them, an Irq resource made as the root and not one",
      "cut to a range, even a range over every line (BadHandle, BadType for a",
      "resource of another kind, AccessDenied for an Irq resource that is not",
